  "name": "serde_bare",
  "description": "A robust implementation of the BARE (Binary Application Record Encoding) format for Rust, leveraging the Serde serialization framework. It provides efficient, non-self-describing binary serialization with native support for variable-length integers and no_std environments. The project ensures protocol interoperability through extensive cross-language benchmarking against Go-based reference implementations.",
